    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0756" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">653.116/123: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal (Caldwell) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-18T18:00:00+00:00">October 18, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 18—2:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Referring to the Legation’s despatch No. 783, January 4, 1933.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d473-f1"/> I am informed unofficially that decrees imposing
                    discriminatory charges have been revoked. Foreign Office advise that new decree
                    on the subject will be published within a few days.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
